{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-b8a374d2e5c0", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:40:00.040Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:40:09.623Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13372, "tokens_out": 104, "latency": 9.559, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Summarise the large loss escalation procedure and the thresholds it uses.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:03a3335983e78cfb388aacd7d1fca08a9ac95fc6ec0b83d66e42b2f51b6e1a5e", "response_text": "I'll search for information about the large loss escalation procedure and its thresholds.", "response_hash": "sha256:78d0042ebaeec90915320e93f9b2fb1548ebd860906fb87dda6fc49c51dbc02b", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-b8a374d2e5c0", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:40:00.040Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:40:09.888Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14641, "tokens_out": 461, "latency": 0.2642, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Summarise the large loss escalation procedure and the thresholds it uses.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:03a3335983e78cfb388aacd7d1fca08a9ac95fc6ec0b83d66e42b2f51b6e1a5e", "response_text": "# Large Loss Escalation Procedure\n\n## Definition and Thresholds\n\nA large loss is defined as any claim where:\n- **Total incurred cost is expected to exceed £100,000**, or\n- **Any claim of any size that carries reputational, regulatory or reinsurance consequences** (prc-largeloss-003)\n\n## Immediate Steps\n\nWithin four working hours of identifying a large loss, handlers must:\n1. Notify the large loss mailbox with claim reference and one-paragraph summary\n2. Set the large loss indicator on the claim record (mandatory, as it drives reinsurance notification and monthly board reporting)\n3. Confirm cover in principle, or record clearly that cover is under investigation (prc-largeloss-003)\n\n## Ownership and Handover\n\n- Large losses transfer to the large loss unit, not handled by the originating team\n- Handover occurs within two working days and includes written notes of all conversations to date (prc-largeloss-003)\n\n## Reinsurance Notification\n\nNotify the reinsurance team where the expected cost **exceeds 50% of the retention for that class**. Retentions are held in the reinsurance treaty summary. Notification should be made on estimate rather than waiting for certainty, as late notification can prejudice recovery (prc-largeloss-003)\n\n## Supplier Appointments and Communication\n\n- Panel suppliers (loss adjusters, solicitors, forensic accountants) can be appointed by the large loss unit without further approval\n- Non-panel suppliers require claims director's written approval, recorded on file\n- One named handler owns all contact with insured, broker and third parties\n- Communications team involved before any statement if press interest is likely (prc-largeloss-003)\n\n## Reporting and Review\n\n- Weekly reporting to claims director; monthly summary to board (including reserve, movement, reason and expected settlement date)\n- Every closed large loss is reviewed within 60 days of closure, examining cost variance and what would have shortened the claim lifecycle (prc-largeloss-003)", "response_hash": "sha256:bccb1c55c424ea0264a12ffd2eb5b306532f7613f08ba257d75ead5d8a36ec63", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
